            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for a spot, then the Kannada for to look splendid."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಯಾತ್ರೆ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯಾತ್ರೆ — yātre — \"a pilgrimage; a long journey\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಜ್ಜಿ ಪ್ರತಿ ವರ್ಷ ಯಾತ್ರೆಗೆ ಹೋಗುತ್ತಾರೆ. ajji prati varṣa yātrege hōguttāre. Grandmother goes on a pilgrimage every year."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯಾತ್ರೆ (yātre) alone can be any long journey; ಯಾತ್ರಿಕ is a pilgrim."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಯಾತ್ರೆ (yātre) is borrowed from Sanskrit yātrā, \"a journey, a festival procession\" (CDIAL 10456), from yā, \"to go\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
