          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕರೆದೊಯ್ಯು — karedoyyu — \"to take along; to escort\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ನಾನು ಅಜ್ಜಿಯನ್ನು ದೇವಸ್ಥಾನಕ್ಕೆ ಕರೆದೊಯ್ದೆ. nānu ajjiyannu dēvasthānakke karedoyde. I took grandmother to the temple."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಕರೆದೊಯ್ದೆ, karedoyde."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕರೆ, to call, plus ಒಯ್ಯು, to take away: to call someone and take them."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಕರೆದೊಯ್ಯು (karedoyyu) is a native Dravidian compound: kare, \"to call\" (DEDR 1291), and oy, \"to carry off, to take along\" (DEDR 984)."
            }
